{
  "title": "T-030 — site_id activation migration: ALTER + backfill 21 operational tables (§9.8, §11.5 V-MS-19, D-MS-14)",
  "prompt": "# T-030 — site_id activation migration\n\nPRD: docs/prd/14-MULTI-SITE-PRD.md §9.8 (table list), §9.9 (composite indexes mandatory pre-activation), §11.5 V-MS-18/19, D-MS-13/14\nProject root: /Users/mariuszkrawczyk/Projects/monopilot-kira\n\n## Goal\nIdempotent, online migration script that activates site_id scoping for the 20 §9.8 operational tables. Each table receives: ALTER ADD COLUMN site_id UUID NULL, CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY (org_id, site_id), backfill to default_site_id, apply site_access_policy_v1 from T-006 generator. Final step transitions state machine 'dual_run' → 'activated'.\n\nThis migration is triggered by `startActivation` Server Action (T-023) as a background job consumed by the worker (T-112 baseline) — large tenants may take minutes to hours.\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. Migration script `packages/db/migrations/0053_site_id_activation.sql` (idempotent):\n   - For each of 21 §9.8 tables (warehouses, license_plates, grn_items, stock_movements, work_orders, wo_outputs, wo_consumptions, wo_dependencies, downtime_events, quality_holds, quality_inspections, ncr_reports, haccp_plans, shipments, sales_orders, inventory_cost_layers, wip_balances, oee_snapshots, maintenance_work_orders, spare_parts_stock, calibration_instruments):\n     - ALTER TABLE IF NOT EXISTS site_id IS NULL (idempotent ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS).\n     - CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS idx_{table}_org_site ON {table}(org_id, site_id) — D-MS-13 mandatory.\n     - Backfill: UPDATE {table} SET site_id = (SELECT id FROM sites WHERE is_default AND org_id={table}.org_id) WHERE site_id IS NULL — done in batched LIMIT 10000 loops to avoid lock storms.\n     - Apply policy via DSL: DROP POLICY IF EXISTS {table}_org_context ON {table}; CREATE POLICY {table}_site_scope ON {table} USING (buildSiteScopedPolicySql generator output from T-006). Generated policies call app.current_site_id() (never raw current_setting GUC) to read site context from the session established by T-001 middleware.\n2. Background job runner `apps/worker/src/jobs/site-id-activation.ts` — chunks by table, reports progress to activation_jobs table (T-017 schema reused).\n3. Final step: UPDATE org_settings SET multi_site_state='activated' WHERE multi_site_state='dual_run'. Write audit_events row 'multisite_activation_completed'.\n4. V-MS-19 post-migration validation query: assert every operational row has site_id = default_site_id (zero NULL site_id in §9.8 tables post-activation).\n5. Tests: idempotent re-run (running twice produces no diff), V-MS-19 100% coverage check, parallel-query test (CONCURRENTLY does not block reads), policy uniformity (every §9.8 table has site_access_policy_v1 variant policy after migration).\n\n## Files\n- packages/db/migrations/0053_site_id_activation.sql [create]\n- apps/worker/src/jobs/site-id-activation.ts [create]\n- apps/worker/src/jobs/__tests__/site-id-activation.test.ts [create]\n- packages/db/__tests__/site-id-activation-integration.test.ts [create]\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n<!-- AC count consolidated from 7→4 by Fixer F14a 2026-05-14 (no coverage lost) -->\n1. Given migration 0053 applied on a clean DB with the 21 §9.8 tables, when re-run, then no diff (idempotent: column already exists, index already exists, policy already applied).\n2. Given a tenant with 1M rows pre-migration in work_orders (NULL site_id), when site-id-activation job runs, then post-job, COUNT(*) WHERE site_id IS NULL == 0 (V-MS-19 100% coverage).\n3. Given 21 §9.8 tables, when post-migration pg_policies inspected, then all 20 have a policy whose USING text equals the output of buildSiteScopedPolicySql({table}) from T-006 (uniformity proven).\n4. Given CONCURRENT writes to license_plates during activation, when activation runs, then writes are not blocked (proven by parallel-write test; only the ALTER COLUMN takes brief AccessExclusiveLock; CONCURRENT index creation does not block).\n5. Given activation_jobs is queried during a run, when polled, then progress per-table is visible (table_name, rows_backfilled, total_rows).\n6. Given activation completes successfully, when org_settings is queried, then multi_site_state='activated' and audit_events has 1 row 'multisite_activation_completed'.\n7. Given activation fails mid-table (e.g. process killed), when re-run, then it resumes from where it left off (no double backfill; idempotent UPDATE).\n\n## Test strategy\n- RED: integration tests for all 7 ACs before migration applied. Use testcontainers Postgres 16; seed 20 tables with realistic row counts.\n- Run 'pnpm --filter @monopilot/db test:integration -- site-id-activation' + 'pnpm --filter @monopilot/web test site-id-activation-job'.\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not use ALTER TABLE without CONCURRENTLY on the index — would block production writes on large tables.\n- Do not backfill with single UPDATE — must batch LIMIT 10000 to avoid bloat + lock storms.\n- Do not skip V-MS-19 post-check — coverage 100% is mandatory before state transitions.\n- Do not transition multi_site_state='activated' if any backfill failed — fail-closed.\n- Do not drop the org-scoped policy before the site-scoped is created — atomic swap per table.\n- Do not skip CodeOwners review — touches 21 operational tables across 9 modules.",
