{
  "title": "T-130 — ESLint enum-lock guard for permissions.enum.ts (RBAC governance)",
  "prompt": "# T-130 — ESLint enum-lock guard for `packages/rbac/src/permissions.enum.ts`\n\n## Goal\nMaterialize the **ESLint enum-lock guard** that every per-module permission-enum task across the monorepo (01-npd T-101, 03-technical T-091, 04-planning-basic T-066, 05-warehouse T-058, 06-scanner-p1 T-049, 07-planning-ext T-058, 08-production T-056, 09-quality T-065, 14-multi-site T-031) currently cites as \"02-settings T-046\". T-046 is in fact `SET-006 Onboarding Completion`; the enum-lock guard does NOT exist yet. This task creates it.\n\nThe guard is a custom ESLint rule `no-direct-permissions-enum-edit` (delivered via the in-repo `tooling/eslint-rules/` workspace) that fails the lint job whenever `packages/rbac/src/permissions.enum.ts` is modified in a way that bypasses the canonical per-module workflow:\n- Add-only edits must come through a PR labelled `permissions-enum-update` AND a corresponding `ALL_<MODULE>_PERMISSIONS` typed export.\n- Renames, deletions, or weakening of the regex `^[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+$` always fail (no escape hatch).\n- The architect-only CODEOWNERS lock on the file (per T-001) remains the human gate; this rule is the **mechanised** gate that prevents merge-by-accident outside the approved label.\n\nPer PRD `docs/prd/02-SETTINGS-PRD.md` §3 [D2] — \"Permission model\" / `permissions.enum.ts` is the single source-of-truth, flat dot-namespaced. The audit `_meta/audits/2026-05-14-permission-enum-addition.md` (RBAC permission-enum batch) declared this guard as a precondition; this task closes that gap.\n\n## Files in scope\n- `tooling/eslint-rules/package.json` [create — name `@monopilot/eslint-rules`, private, workspace package]\n- `tooling/eslint-rules/src/no-direct-permissions-enum-edit.ts` [create — ESLint rule implementation]\n- `tooling/eslint-rules/src/index.ts` [create — re-exports + plugin manifest]\n- `tooling/eslint-rules/src/__tests__/no-direct-permissions-enum-edit.test.ts` [create — `RuleTester` (eslint) suite]\n- `tooling/eslint-rules/tsconfig.json` [create]\n- `packages/rbac/.eslintrc.cjs` [create or modify — register the plugin and enable the rule as `error`]\n- `apps/web/.eslintrc.cjs` [modify — add `@monopilot/eslint-rules/no-direct-permissions-enum-edit` to the root config so `apps/web` import paths still trigger]\n- `pnpm-workspace.yaml` [modify — add `tooling/eslint-rules` to the workspaces list if not already covered by a wildcard]\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` [modify — ensure `pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules test` runs in the lint job (or piggy-backs on the root `pnpm test` matrix)]\n\n## Implementation contract\n1. **Rule semantics** — `no-direct-permissions-enum-edit` runs on every file lint pass. It does NOT do anything when the file under lint is anything other than `packages/rbac/src/permissions.enum.ts`. When it IS that file:\n   - Scan all top-level statements. If any export adds a string literal value whose dotted form fails the canonical regex `^[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+$`, report `permissions-enum-regex-violation` with the offending value.\n   - Detect rename/delete by comparing against a checked-in baseline at `tooling/eslint-rules/baselines/permissions.snapshot.json` — entries that disappear OR change their literal string fail with `permissions-enum-illegal-removal`.\n   - If an `ALL_<MODULE>_PERMISSIONS` export is added, require: (a) it is a `readonly Permission[]` typed array literal, and (b) every element is also present in the parent `Permission` const. Failures report `permissions-enum-orphan-array`.\n   - The PR-label gate is **CI-side**, NOT inside the rule (we can't read GitHub labels from ESLint). Instead the rule is `severity: error` always; the CI job under `.github/workflows/ci.yml` is the gate that decides whether to short-circuit by reading the `permissions-enum-update` label. Document this clearly in the rule docstring.\n2. **Plugin packaging** — `tooling/eslint-rules` exports `module.exports = { rules: { 'no-direct-permissions-enum-edit': ruleImpl } }`. Add `\"@monopilot/eslint-rules\": \"workspace:*\"` to `packages/rbac/package.json` devDependencies.\n3. **Baseline snapshot** — On first run (or via `pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules snapshot` script), regenerate `permissions.snapshot.json` from the current `permissions.enum.ts`. Snapshot is checked in; updates must accompany approved enum-update PRs.\n4. **Tests** — `RuleTester` from `eslint`. Cases:\n   - VALID: a snapshotted file unchanged.\n   - VALID: a snapshotted file with an appended `npd.gate.approve` (matches regex AND present in `Permission`) AND a matching `ALL_NPD_PERMISSIONS` array.\n   - INVALID: snapshot has `npd.gate.approve`, file removes it → `permissions-enum-illegal-removal`.\n   - INVALID: file adds `npd.gate` (2 segments) → `permissions-enum-regex-violation`.\n   - INVALID: file adds `npd.gate.approve` but no entry exists in `Permission` const → `permissions-enum-orphan-array` (when consumed via the `ALL_<MODULE>_PERMISSIONS` array literal).\n   - VALID: any OTHER file (e.g. `packages/rbac/src/role-mappings.ts`) → rule no-ops.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (Given-When-Then)\n<!-- F15-consolidation 2026-05-14: 7 ACs fused to 4 via strict-subset fusion (F6/F8 patterns). AC5+AC1→AC1, AC2+AC3→AC2, AC4→AC3, AC7+AC6→AC4. All assertions remain testable. -->\n- AC1 — Given the rule is loaded against any file other than `packages/rbac/src/permissions.enum.ts`, when lint runs, then the rule no-ops with zero reports; AND given `permissions.enum.ts` is unmodified and matches the checked-in snapshot, then `pnpm --filter @monopilot/rbac lint` also reports zero violations.\n- AC2 — Given a developer renames or deletes an existing key in `permissions.enum.ts` without updating the snapshot, when lint runs, then the rule emits `permissions-enum-illegal-removal` with severity `error` and exits non-zero; AND given a developer appends a string that fails the regex `^[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+$` (e.g. two-segment `npd.new_capability`), then the rule emits `permissions-enum-regex-violation` with severity `error`.\n- AC3 — Given a developer adds a string to `ALL_<MODULE>_PERMISSIONS` but does NOT add it to the parent `Permission` const, when lint runs, then the rule emits `permissions-enum-orphan-array` with severity `error`.\n- AC4 — Given `pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules vitest run` executes, then all `RuleTester` cases listed in `Implementation contract` §4 pass; AND given the PR carries the `permissions-enum-update` label AND the snapshot is regenerated via `pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules snapshot`, when CI re-runs, then both rule and CI gate accept the change.\n\n## Test strategy (RED-first, runnable commands)\n1. RED: write `tooling/eslint-rules/src/__tests__/no-direct-permissions-enum-edit.test.ts` covering all AC cases via ESLint's `RuleTester` + parallel vitest harness. Run:\n   `pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules vitest run`\n   — expect failure.\n2. GREEN: implement the rule, plugin manifest, baseline snapshot, and registration in `packages/rbac/.eslintrc.cjs`. Re-run the same command — expect pass.\n3. Run `pnpm --filter @monopilot/rbac lint` against an unmodified `permissions.enum.ts` — expect zero violations (AC1).\n4. Run the integration assertion: temporarily delete one entry from `permissions.enum.ts`, re-run `pnpm --filter @monopilot/rbac lint`, observe the `permissions-enum-illegal-removal` error, then revert.\n5. Run `pnpm typecheck` for `@monopilot/eslint-rules` and `@monopilot/rbac` packages.\n\n## Risk red lines\n- Do not weaken the canonical regex `^[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+\\.[a-z_]+$` — it must remain the literal source of truth in the rule body.\n- Do not allow the rule to silently no-op on `permissions.enum.ts` due to a missing snapshot file; if the snapshot is missing, FAIL with a clear actionable message (`run: pnpm --filter @monopilot/eslint-rules snapshot`).\n- Do not add a CLI escape hatch (`// eslint-disable-next-line`) that disables this rule — the rule MUST be marked `meta.docs.recommended: true` and the package README must instruct reviewers to reject PRs that include the disable comment for this rule.\n- Do not depend on GitHub API calls or labels at lint time — label enforcement is a CI-job concern.\n- Do not introduce a parallel permission registry file (no `packages/rbac/src/*PermissionEnum.ts`); the enum file remains the single source of truth.\n- Do not commit a generated snapshot that omits any existing keys — snapshot updates must be additive and reviewer-verified.\n\n## Closeout evidence required\n- changed_files (with line counts)\n- exact test commands and outputs (RED→GREEN, vitest pass, `pnpm --filter @monopilot/rbac lint`)\n- acceptance_criteria_status (one row per AC1..AC7)\n- deviations_from_prd (or \"none\")\n- git_status\n- One end-to-end demo showing AC2 by intentionally renaming an entry and observing CI fail (gif or terminal capture stored under `_meta/handoffs/T-130-closeout/`).\n\nStack: TS + ESLint (>=9 flat-config compatible) + vitest + pnpm workspaces. Plugin built as a workspace package alongside `packages/rbac`.\n",
